<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=sewing-needle">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Tools and materials</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sewing needle</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A sewing needle is a slender pointed tool with an eye at one end to carry thread through material. A needle of bird bone found in Denisova Cave and attributed to the Denisovans is estimated to be about 50,000 years old, and a bone needle from Potok Cave in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slovenia">Slovenia</a> dates to the Aurignacian, 47,000 to 41,000 years ago. Bone and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a> needles come from Xiaogushan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liaoning">Liaoning</a> and from Kostenki in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, and Flinders Petrie found <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> sewing needles at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naqada">Naqada</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> dating from 4400 to 3000 BCE. Iron needles are known from the third century BCE, and needle-making began at Redditch in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1639.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sewing-needle.jpg" alt="Sewing needle" width="330" height="189" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Didier Descouens · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aiguille_os_246.1_Global.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 50,000 years ago</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Denisova Cave</dd></div></dl><p class="inv-entry-note"><span class="inv-k">Note</span>Bone awls from Blombos Cave in southern Africa date to 73,000–70,000 years ago, and a point from Sibudu Cave in South Africa, 61,000 years old, might be from a bone needle.</p><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=sewing-needle">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
